# ci-apt.sh runs on the Linux runners, and as root through sudo once `prepare`
# has copied it to /usr/local/bin as apt-fast. A CRLF shebang is
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which the kernel resolves to a nonexistent
# interpreter, and every lane of ci.yml would then lose its apt step. This repo
# is developed from a Windows box where `core.autocrlf=true`, so the
# normalisation happens by config rather than by rule; this makes it a rule
# (the root .gitattributes does the same for scripts/*.sh).
*.sh text eol=lf
